("The Project method was developed by:",["W.H. Kilpatrick","H.E. Armstrong","Helen Parkhurst","Fred Keller"],"Kilpatrick (1918), following Dewey."),
("In UGC's 10-point grading scale under CBCS, grade 'A+' stands for:",["Excellent, 9 points","Outstanding, 10 points","Very Good, 8 points","Good, 7 points"],"O=10 Outstanding, A+=9 Excellent, A=8 Very Good."),
("A test that gives consistent results on repeated administration is said to have:",["Reliability","Validity","Objectivity","Usability"],"Consistency = reliability."),
