("Match the following:\nList I: (a) Remember (b) Analyse (c) Valuing (d) Naturalisation\nList II: (i) Psychomotor domain (ii) Affective domain (iii) Lowest cognitive level (revised) (iv) Higher cognitive level",["a-iii, b-iv, c-ii, d-i","a-iv, b-iii, c-ii, d-i","a-iii, b-iv, c-i, d-ii","a-ii, b-iv, c-iii, d-i"],"Remember is lowest; Valuing is affective; Naturalisation is Dave's psychomotor level."),
('AR', "Reflective level teaching is the highest level of teaching.", "It develops problem-solving, critical and creative thinking in learners.", 0, "Both true; R explains why it is highest."),
('AR', "A valid test is always reliable.", "Reliability is a necessary condition for validity.", 0, "Without consistency a test cannot measure accurately, so validity needs reliability."),
